 ## Overview
-Gradient Scaling by Distance Squared is a technique applied during the backpropagation phase of training ray compositing to improve training stability for distant objects [S1, unofficial]. It scales the gradients of field outputs based on the squared distance of samples from the camera [S1, unofficial]. As a child of Training Ray Compositing (Sigma) [3868-training-ray-compositing-sigma.md], it addresses gradient magnitude imbalances along rays by weighting parameter updates with sample depth.
